# The same as if on an M1 MacBook Air's 2880 x 1800 picture (DM_TEST_SCREEN_PX): even 3D 50% doesn't fit at Native, so Recommended takes a smaller output: 1600 wide, the 3D at 100%, the present enlarging it with MetalFX, and
# Frame Generation on. Temporal and the interpolator at a fixed output below the screen's, the combination only slow Macs and the Performance preset reach.
name pic_mac_firstboot_m1_air
requires mac-app
save warlock
timeout 300
env DM_TEST_VIDEO_FIRSTBOOT=1 "DM_TEST_GPU_NAME=Apple M1" DM_TEST_GPU_CORES=8 DM_TEST_SCREEN_PX=2880x1800 DM_GAME_SEED=305419896

expect main_menu timeout=120
enter_game
sleep 8
screenshot m1_air.png
system_quit
check no_red
check no_red_log
check event picture how=first mode=1 res=0 up=2 aa=1 aniso=3 color=1 s3d=0 envsh=1 shq=2 fg=1 envd=1 rt=0
check log_has "→ Recommended fixed 1600, 3D 100%, environment shadows on, shadows Ultra, Frame Drops lower, Frame Generation on"
check log_has "temporal scaler: .* built in"
check log_has "frame generation: interpolator .* built in"
